@startuml

start

:Embedded control platform employs RTOS;
:Supervisory finite-state machine scheduled via periodic timer interrupts;
fork
  :Orchestrate high-priority ISRs for data acquisition;
fork again
  :Orchestrate lower-priority tasks for deferred processing;
end fork

if (Detect anomalous physiological data?) then (yes)
fork
  :Validate signal integrity via CRC check;
  :Initiate diagnostic state sequence;
  fork
    :Confirm electrocardiogram fluctuations;
  fork again
    :Classify events;
  fork again
    :Assess risk of ventricular tachycardia;
  end fork
fork again
  :Dedicated task synchronized using mutex-protected ring buffer;
  :Commence high-frequency ECG data logging to non-volatile storage;
end fork

  :Dispatch two parallel processes managed by priority-based scheduler;
  fork
    :High-priority task;
    :Initiate exponential backoff algorithm;
    :Transmit alarm notifications to medical staff over CAN bus;
  fork again
    :Lower-priority task;
    :Perform real-time signal processing on collected parameters;
  end fork

  :Watchdog timer monitors health of concurrent operation;

  :Final arbitration state evaluates all results;
  if (Activate first aid program?) then (yes)
    :Trigger first aid program;
  else (no)
  end if

  :Asynchronously upload final diagnosis to medical data center via secure channel;
  :Update patient's electronic medical record;

  if (All anomalies resolved?) then (yes)
    :Halt monitoring iteration;
    :Return to low-power standby state managed by PMIC;
    :Persist all events to structured log for audit and post-analysis;
  else (no)
  end if

else (no)
end if

stop

@enduml
